Full-metric affine NVF cell validation, 2026-09-09

Environment: Darwin arm64; Python 3.12; NumPy 2.5.1; SciPy 1.18.0;
JAX 0.11.0 with x64; Torch 2.13.0.
Invocations set PYTHONPATH to the checkout and OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1,
OMP_NUM_THREADS=1. These settings do not establish Apple Accelerate's
actual thread count. Elapsed times include concurrent validation processes.

Scope
-----
Affine images of the existing reference rectangle/strip profile, with
full spatial metric, mixed weak equations, exact laminated contact lift,
sesquilinear Fourier projection and physical Cartesian matrix export.
The public physical-rectangle adapter retains its orthogonal-point-lattice
contract. No Li substitution, regularization, clipping or new optical
acceptance threshold is introduced.

Affine kernel and engine controls
--------------------------------
python -m pytest tests/test_nvf_affine_cell.py -q --tb=short
54 passed in 38.75s.
This includes independent tensor projection, diagonal-kernel equivalence,
real/complex laminated contact, graded-y and ungraded-y covariance,
passive Fourier forms, three engine backends, and four JAX controls.

python -m pytest tests/test_nvf_affine_cell.py -q -k 'diagonal_metric or physical_rotation' --tb=short
28 passed, 30 deselected in 2.11s after adding the maximum supported
body/gap degree pair (4,6) and an explicit positive-gap unit-mean field
assertion. Four cases are new; 24 repeat the preceding run.
Distinct affine test cases: 58.

