Stabilized contact opening under x refinement (2026-09-10)
The original INITIAL_X4_GUARD_FAILURE above remains a failed pre-JAX checkpoint.
The new independent oracle forms local r before adding the physical origin,
uses Kahan weak products, and refines against compensated original-system
residuals. Each trace/body solve shares one balanced LU for the initial solve
and three corrections (four inverse applications). Equations, quadrature,
finite spaces, production source hashes and all three guards are unchanged.
The integrated oracle matches the separately validated arithmetic prototype
exactly. The new complete records reuse original x1/x2 JAX arrays only after
matching all seven production source hashes and family/settings metadata and
comparing them anew to the current independent oracle. Only x4 JAX is new.
All nine components of each reference/production array were saved before audit.
Nested integrated_oracle_metadata retains its earlier references_complete
state and oracle-only scope; the enclosing record reports the later JAX audit.
Archive paths and executable locations are omitted; hashes retain identities.
